#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# hyper_harmonic_number

#% text
# `hyper_harmonic_number(r, m)` gives the hyperharmonic number: H(0, m) = 1/m and H(r, m) = H(r - 1, 1) + ... + H(r - 1, m).

#% text
# `hyper_harmonic_number(r, m, s)` starts from H(0, m) = 1/m^s.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For integers it is `binomial(m + r - 1, r - 1) (harmonic_number(m + r - 1) - harmonic_number(r - 1))`; at inexact arguments `gamma(m + r)/(gamma(m + 1) gamma(r)) (digamma(m + r) - digamma(r))`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
hyper_harmonic_number(2, 4)
#% output
#= 77/12

#% cell
table(hyper_harmonic_number(3, k), [k, 6])
#% output
#= [1, 7/2, 47/6, 57/4, 459/20, 341/10]

#% cell
hyper_harmonic_number(1, 4.0 + im)
#% output
#= 2.107160103171069 + 0.2178505180568165im

#% cell
hyper_harmonic_number(3, 4, 2)
#% output
#= 571/48

